        </p>
        <dl class="ledger-row">
          <div><dt>Test</dt><dd><code>test_csv.sh</code> &ldquo;export runs&rdquo;</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Detects</dt><dd><code>--csv</code> exits non-zero</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Covered by</dt><dd>No other test</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Verdict</dt><dd>Kept. &ldquo;Name is weak, assertion is not.&rdquo;</dd></div>
        </dl>
        <p>
          I had meant to plant an empty test and planted a useful one. I changed
          the fixture so the test ends in <code>; true</code> and truly
          can&rsquo;t fail. The audit now removes it, and names the stronger test
          that covers the same failure.
        </p>
      </Reveal>

      <figure class="post-panel" aria-label="One request, two results. Before a fix to the skill, the agent wrote six browser tests and no unit test, and scored 0.43. After the fix it wrote unit tests for the rules and reported a boundary bug, and scored 0.89. Without the plugin the score was 0.36.">
